From: danilo neves cruz <cruzdanilo@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 23:44:37 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix: read Android hierarchies without waiting for idle

Each view hierarchy read first waited for the device to go 500 ms without accessibility events, up to 500 ms. Android sends content changes at most every 100 ms, so an app that changed anything in the last half second, as it does right after every tap, made each read wait its full 500 ms, and a settle needs at least two reads. Callers that need a stable screen already compare consecutive reads until two match, so read right away.
---
 .../androidTest/java/dev/mobile/maestro/MaestroDriverService.kt  | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/maestro-android/src/androidTest/java/dev/mobile/maestro/MaestroDriverService.kt b/maestro-android/src/androidTest/java/dev/mobile/maestro/MaestroDriverService.kt
index 9e75fec..df3b277 100644
--- a/maestro-android/src/androidTest/java/dev/mobile/maestro/MaestroDriverService.kt
+++ b/maestro-android/src/androidTest/java/dev/mobile/maestro/MaestroDriverService.kt
@@ -243,7 +243,6 @@ class Service(
      */
     private fun refreshAccessibilityCache() {
         try {
-            uiDevice.waitForIdle(500)
             uiAutomation.serviceInfo = null
         } catch (nullExp: NullPointerException) {
             /* no-op */
